- runtime/somart/codec.py      NumPy port of motionbricks/model/soma/kernels.py and
                               motionbricks/model/kernels.py (encode, decode, conditions,
                               endpoint correction)
- runtime/somart/skeleton.py   BVH loading logic ported from motionbricks/io/bvh.py
- runtime/somart/contract.py   constants from motionbricks/model/contract.py and soma_n1.json

The upstream ONNX exporter (tools/onnx) is used unmodified from third_party/ (not redistributed).
Changes relative to upstream: vectorised NumPy implementation, batching, and the additional
velocity-matching and contact-aware options in codec.py.

Model weights: NVIDIA Open Model Agreement ("Licensed by NVIDIA Corporation under the NVIDIA Open
Model License"). site/models/ holds an INT8-quantized derivative for the web demo, stored in a split GGUF file
whose INT8 matrix weights are re-coded with ggml Q5_0 blocks (tools/gguf/build_gguf.py).
Sample motion clips: NVIDIA Sample Data Evaluation License. The clips are not redistributed here;
site/data/windows.* contains motion windows derived from them (internal evaluation use).
SOMA body mesh (site/data/soma_mesh.*): extracted from the upstream MotionBricks asset
soma_base_skel_minimal_no_root.usd, NVIDIA, CC BY 4.0.

site/data/clips.* (clips named 100STYLE/*) and site/data/styles/*: motion capture from the 100STYLE dataset by
Ian Mason, Sebastian Starke and Taku Komura, "Real-Time Style Modelling of Human Locomotion via Feature-Wise
Transformations and Local Motion Phases" (2022), https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.8127870, licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Modified: retargeted onto the SOMA rig, trimmed with the
dataset's frame cuts, resampled to 30 fps and quantized (tools/mocap/style100.py, tools/export_web_data.py).

site/vendor/ redistributes, unmodified: onnxruntime-web 1.31.1 (Microsoft, MIT), three.js 0.170.0
(MIT, including addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js and addons/utils/BufferGeometryUtils.js);
site/coi-serviceworker.js (Guido Zuidhof, MIT). Licence texts are in site/vendor/.


site/models/balanced/motionbricks-*.gguf, shard 1 (animal network): weights trained in this repository
(tools/animal/train_mann.py, packed by tools/gguf/build_gguf.py) on the
dog motion capture of Zhang, Starke, Komura and Saito, "Mode-Adaptive Neural Networks for Quadruped Motion
Control" (SIGGRAPH 2018), https://github.com/sebastianstarke/AI4Animation, licensed CC BY-NC 4.0. The weights
are a derivative of that data: non-commercial use only, with attribution. The raw data is not redistributed.

